ic (e.g., top-1 accuracy, MRR, directional asymmetry index), and the controls (name frequency, gender, alias, multiple children per parent, deceased status, half-siblings, in-laws). (4) Assumptions and uncertainties: list each assumption (e.g., availability of a celebrity name-pair file, choice of model), the source supporting it, the consequence if it is wrong, and the mitigation. Flag specifically: how source-supported the hypothesis of directional bias is, how 'celebrity' and 'parent-child' will be defined and verified, and how prompt framing will be controlled to avoid trivially cueing the answer. Do not start drafting the full experimental protocol yet — we will refine at approach_review.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"For real-world factual data on celebrity parent-child relationships, LLMs will exhibit a directional bias by accurately retrieving a parent when given a child’s name, but will underperform when trying to retrieve the child given the parent.\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
