 Sensitivity analysis: re-run DAI within tier-A pairs and within non-tier-A pairs; require consistency before claiming directional bias. |\\n| A4 | \\\"Parent / child\\\" relationships are unambiguous in the test pairs. | Assumption; rules exclude half-siblings, step/adopted, in-laws, contested paternity. | Mislabeled gold reduces accuracy in both directions symmetrically (bias toward null, not toward the hypothesized direction). | Apply the same exclusion rules in both directions; report N_excluded and a sensitivity check that includes ambiguous cases. |\\n| A5 | Prompt framing can be made directionally parallel without cueing the answer. | Assumption; standard practice in paired-prompt designs. | An asymmetric cue (e.g., role-naming) could manufacture apparent bias. | Parallel template audit; neutral-keyword version vs. role-cued version; require that the between-version discrepancy be small. |\\n| A6 | Closed-set k-way MCQ with matched distractors is a fair scoring format. | Assumption; standard in LLM factual-recall benchmarks. | Possible; ceiling/floor effects, distractor-strength asymmetry across directions. | Pilot on a small calibration subset; require that distractor-pool difficulty is matched across directions by human-rated difficulty (offline rubric). |\\n| A7 | Two comparable model families at similar parameter scale can be specified without listing exact checkpoints. | Assumption (design-only deliverable). | Deferring the choice blocks pre-registration of compute needs. | Researcher picks the two families at approach_review; debias by parameter count and training data overlap where possible (e.g., family pairs). |\\n| A8 | All evaluation code is expressible in Python stdlib (no `numpy`, `scipy`). | Verified by `pip list` \\u2014 neither installed and offline. | If a dependency is later deemed necessary, installation will fail. | Use stdlib `statistics` for CIs, a hand-rolled paired bootstrap over pairs, and a Wilcoxon-style sign test that requires only counts. |\\n\\n**Uncertainties explicitly flagged for the researcher to resolve at approach_review**\\n1. **How source-supported is the directional-bias hypothesis?** \\u2014 Not source-supported offline (no citations fetchable). The proposed design treats it as a falsifiable pre-registered hypothesis with a stated null, not as established prior.\\n2. **How will \\\"celebrity\\\" and \\\"parent-child\\\" be defined and verified?** \\u2014 Proposed offline operationalization in A2\\u2013A4 above; requires researcher confirmation or amendment (e.g., should we use a different fame proxy, or restrict to a single domain such as film/TV?).\\n3. **How will prompt framing be controlled to avoid trivially cueing the answer?** \\u2014 Parallel template + neutral-keyword vs. role-cued sanity check, as in A5; requires researcher sign-off on the exact wording at approach_review.\\n\\n## Proposed next step (no execution)\\nAt `approach_review`, the researcher and I will refine: target N pairs, exact model family slots, exact prompt templates (neutral vs. role-cued), tie-breaking rule for parents with several famous children, and the precise pre-registered primary metric (proposal: paired DAI = Acc_C\\u2192P \\u2212 Acc_P\\u2192C, with bootstrap 95% CI; sign test as the inferential test). Awaiting explicit approval before drafting the full experimental protocol.\", \"evidence\": \"**Repository inspection (executed exploratory commands, exit 0):**\\n- `ls -la /workspace` \\u2192 single file `task.json` (537 bytes).\\n- `find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type f` and `-maxdepth 4` \\u2192 only `/workspace/task.json`.\\n- `find /workspace -name \\\"track.md\\\"` \\u2192 no output (file absent).\\n- `pip list | grep -iE \\\"torch|transformers|sentence|vllm|llama|openai|sklearn|numpy|pandas|scipy|datasets|huggingface|tokenizers\\\"` \\u2192 0 matches; only `requests 2.31.0`, `urllib3 2.0.7` matched the looser pattern.\\n- `python3 --version` \\u2192 `Python 3.12.3`; `pip --version` \\u2192 `pip 24.0`.\\n- `curl https://pypi.org/simple/ ` \\u2192 DNS failure (`Could not resolve host`), confirming network disabled.\\n\\n**Documentation evidence:**\\n- `/workspace/task.json` field `documents.track.md` content (verbatim): \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"\\n- `task.json` supplies the hypothesis as the public task question; no URLs, no datasets, no models, no prior notes are preloaded.\\n\\n**Design-only constraint adherence:**\\n- No experiment was executed. No fabricated numbers, reference IDs, or celebrity name pairs were introduced. All name-dependent specifics are deferred to the procedural generator + researcher-curated seed, both of which the researcher can inspect or override.\", \"assumptions\": [\"A public-task directional-bias hypothesis is being treated as a pre-registered, falsifiable hypothesis rather than established prior, because no citation could be fetched (network disabled) to source-verify it.\", \"A small hand-curated seed of ~100\\u2013150 high-confidence celebrity parent-child pairs can be authored offline with sufficient label quality.\", \"\\\"Celebrity\\\" can be operationalized offline via a static fame-tier table (bucketed pageview tertiles from a fixed baseline month) replicated inside the repo.\", \"\\\"Parent / child\\\" relationships can be made unambiguous by excluding half-siblings, step/adopted, in-laws, and contested cases, in both directions symmetrically.\", \"Prompt framing can be made parallel and non-cueing across directions; a neutral-keyword vs. role-cued sanity check is feasible offline.\", \"Two comparable open-weight model families can be named at approach_review without constraining the choice in advance.\", \"All evaluation code is expressible in Python stdlib (`json`, `csv`, `random`, `statistics`, `itertools`, `collections`, `math`, `re`) \\u2014 `numpy`/`scipy` are not installed and cannot be fetched.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Borderline relationship cases (step/adopted/half-sibling) for some celebrity pairs are likely; final inclusion/exclusion rule needs researcher confirmation.\", \"Choice of open-weight model families (and whether to include a base vs. instruction-tuned contrast) is open and affects effect-size interpretability.\", \"Offspring ambiguity when a parent has multiple famous children (e.g., Will Smith \\u2192 Jaden / Willow) needs a pre-registered tie-breaking rule (e.g., gold = most-associated child across both directions).\", \"Whether distractor pools can be difficulty-matched across directions using only offline rubricjudging; if not, results may conflate direction with distractor-difficulty asymmetry.\", \"Whether \\\"child\\\" vs. \\\"offspring\\\" vs. \\\"son/daughter\\\" lexical variants should be used; this could itself induce a direction effect and must be locked at approach_review.\", \"Exact N needed to power a paired sign test on a moderate effect (e.g., \\u0394 accuracy \\u2248 0.10) at \\u03b1=0.05, \\u03b2=0.20 \\u2014 needs pre-registration against expected baseline accuracy.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-f833bc3a-b23a-4502-bc27-892a3cfc13a8", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
